        <p>OAR ACCIDENT NARITO-W-L. T.—AVERTED -John Baguley hawker, 6i, Boatook-street. was charge i with furiously driv- ing a horse nd lorry in Bridge-street on April usth. -He pleaded guilty.-P 0 Casey stated that he was ow point duty in Hylands-street on the .date named whoa he saw I d fondant driving a Morse sod lorry at a very furious rate He called upon him to step as a car.' was leaving Rylands-sf reef, but he did not do so, and the driver had to put on full speed to avoid a coltlsion.-Mr Healey, tramway inspector, said he was at H vlan Is street terminus as the 4.25 cur wss leaving and he eavr the defend- ant driving down Bridit•-stree at a furious rate. He refused to stop and witness told the car driver to 40 aheu i to try and avoid a collision The air Ras then put oa to the rate o' about 12 or 14 miles an hour to et cut of the way. In p%tting on speed like Haut It ne d•lv pal el the wires down -The Chief Constable ffairl that defendant had b usi bemre th - court 46 times lu thu narrow streets the gre 'test care had to he ex.rcised by all perso.se an I most of all by drivers. -liilefeodant was fined ii. and costs.</p>
