      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-05-09_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>Drowning Fatality at Widnes.</head>
        <p>Drowning Fatality at Widnes.</p>
        <p>Mr Samuel Brighouse, coroner, held an inquest at the Accident Hospital, on Monday afternoon on the body of Walter Sandhach, eked fliteen, • 57, Uhol- mondelay-streer, son of a gar eman at Widnes Dock. Deceasediand another boy on Friday evening got into a podtoon on the Rankey and St Helens Clue' near Hutchinson's works, anicommenced to row on the canal. Deceased bad possession of the oar, and was standing up, when it slipped out of the row- lock, and he fell lute the wat•tr. His companion went for assistance, but Sendtlach sank befare it arrived. Some twenty minutes afterwards Sergeant Ratcliffe got the body to the surface. Artificial respiration was resorted to, but without success. A vsraict of " Accidental death " was returned, and a vote of sympathy was accorded to the parents.</p>
      </div>
