      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-05-09_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <head>ORNIWAMS' PINK MS FOR PALE PEOPLE</head>
        <p>ORNIWAMS' PINK MS FOR PALE PEOPLE</p>
        <p>No medicine ever discovered has effected so many wonderful cures. And the cured people remain well.</p>
        <p>WORK BECOMES A DRAG.</p>
        <p>A Lancashire Woman's Remedy.</p>
        <p>"1 have always been fairly light-hearted, so far as circumstances allowed," said a lady living at 12, Dyson-street, Blackburn, to the "Blackburn Standard ' special correspondent, the other day ; "but about six years ago a sad change came over me. My household duties became ajdrag and a toil, and in a very few days I was helpless, and could not do my housework; indeed, I should be still idle but for the splendid results achieved in my case. by rr Williams' pink pills for pale people. I had aching pains all day long, and at night I was unable to sleep. I tried all sorts of remedies. But I only grew worse and worse, and with a heavy heart I sent for the best doctor I knew of, who told me I had sciatica, and gave me some medicine. I sank lower and lower, however, and I really thought my case was hopeless. One day my daughter came home and said she had hoard a great deal about people being cured by taking Dr Williams pink pills for pale people. I ridiculed the idea of their curing me, but consented to her fetching a box from the nearest chemist. When I had finished the box I felt down-hearted, for I was not much, if any, better, and at first I refused to allow my daughter to et another box. She persisted, however, saying I should give them a fair trial, and before I had half finished the second box I felt like a new woman. I finished the box, and was cured as completely as anyone could wish to be. What is more, I have not had an attack of the complaint since."</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-05-09_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>INDIGESTION FOR YEARS.</head>
        <p>INDIGESTION FOR YEARS.</p>
        <p>Lancashire Woman's Cure of a Painful Complaint.</p>
        <p>Well within sound of the bells of St. Francis of Assisi, at Gorton, Manchester an event has just occurred which concerns chiefly a Mrs. Lowe,tand a representative of the "Ashton Reporter,' recently waited upon Mrs. Lowe at her residence, 70, Rosebery-street, off Queen's-road, to glean the facts. " Yes," she said, "I have suffered much from indigestion for years, and would be suffering still if I had not taken Dr. Williams pink pills for pale people. Years ago I had the complaint, and was under one doctor and then another, but the improvement was not very marked. In April, last year, I began to be very bad. I had pains in my head and stomach, and:across my back, and I could not take my food. I then went to two medical men ; but I do not think I made much progress under .their treatment.". _</p>
        <p>. - "I was told that I was completely run down. You would not recognise me if you had seen me before. I was thin, pale and nervous, through lack of the nourish- ment which the severe indigestion prevented me taking. I had been at home about a month when I was recommended to try Dr. Williams' pink pills for pale people. I did try them; I found that they did me good, and I have continued to take them ever since. I began to feel relief after I had taken the contents of the second box. They have done me a world of good, "she added, enthusiastically. "Nothing ails me now."</p>
        <p>Dr. Williams' Pink Pills make new blood and have cured Consumption and "Decline," Neuralgia, Skin Disorders, Anemia, Indigestion; Rheumatism, Kidney Diseases, After-Ejects of Influenza, St. Vitus' Dance, Paralysis, Locomotor Ataxy, Palpitation, and Disorders of Women. If you are pestered to buy substitutes, you can have a box direct from Di.. Williams' Medicine Co. Holborn Viaduct, London, post free, for 2S. 9d., Or six boxes for 135. 9d.</p>
