        <p>HATTON SEWERAGE. Mr James Dias, water and salwary engineer to the Warrington Corporation wrote fiad there is atdt a good deal of sewage fiadiug its way into Hatton Brook which indicates that there is still a good deal of pro- perty in Hattor. act yet connected up to the sewer, and I shall be obliged if you will bring prelsuri to bear at once on the owners of property ; oth-u.wise the money expendtd on the new outfall sewer by the Corporation have been wasted so far as the Corporatioa are con- cerned." The Clerk stated that he bad sent the letter to the sur- veyor and the ma t.r was rviw receiviag his attention. THE PIPING OF WEASTE-LANE DITCH, A letter was received from the Local Government Board adverting to a letter sent by Mr Leah, Cuerdea Stables, which has aopeared in the local papers and which had since been sent to the Bard, asking that I tne Board be informed as to the progress made in piping the ditches in question. • The Clerk stated that be had replied to the Local Government Board to the effct that the piping for the ditch was in progress</p>
        <p>A-NUISANCE AT FRODSHANI. Mr T Leicester, manager tor Messrs f Rigby ayd Son, Frodsham Bridge, wrote drawing attention to an open drain or sewer which runs from some cottages, through the firm's groubd,just by the corner of Frodsham Bridge, and discharges into the river. The smell from this was very bad at times, especially in summer. It was close to the high road, and was a great nuisance to them. They suggested something chould be done to effect an improvement. Resolved that the matter be referred to the Sutton Parochial Committee.</p>
