        <head>Cemetery.</head>
        <p>The Cemetery.</p>
        <p>Mr It abert Young, registrar at the CAmetery, has submitted his forty fifth annual report,tor the year ending March 31st, 1902. The receipts, 'amount to £1,233 Ils lid; corresponding period last year, £1,264 2s 7d. There have ben interred during the past year 1,187 adults and minors, and 142 still- born children and premature ; correspondin:z num- ber len year, 1,215 adults and minors, and 128 still- born children and premature, howing a decrease of 28 burials and an increase of 14 stilloorn-,and a decrease in receipts of £3O 10a 81, The Vacancy in the Whitecroas Ward.</p>
        <p>Two candidates were nominated to supply the casual Tacancy in the ahoy. ward occasioned by the death of Councillor Plunapton, namely, Mr Thomar, Barton (Liberal), gentleman, 102, Lovely- lane, and Mr William Throssell (Independent), 49, •Lovely-lane,wine and spirit merchant. Mr Throseell withdrew his ncmination shortly before two o'clock on Saturday afternoon, and the result is that Mr Barton is returned uno posed.</p>
