        <p>The five minutes within which the Bishop of London must confine hi 6i sermon at the Coronation is (the "Daily Chronicle" states) just one-fourth of dui • time usually allowed to preachers before royalty. Like Q leen VAetoria his Mrjesty dislikes a sermon to exceed wenty minutes, and forbids any reference to current political evente. Onelof the first cares of the Germany Eaveror wag to abbreviate his chaplains—or rather their sermons. A full hour is occupied by the e renon in the ordinary Lutheran serric., but this the Law rat' in a hotly reduced to a mere twenty minutee,except when he him- self takes the pulpit. Napoeleon III: was more generous by ten =flutes, but if the sermon promised to exceed half an hour an official of the court stepped forward and stood before the altar as a warning to conclude the die- course, which was then wound up in all haste.</p>
