      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-05-09_WidnesExaminer_art0114" n="art0114">
        <head>VICE-CHAIRMANSHIP.</head>
        <p>THE VICE-CHAIRMANSHIP.</p>
        <p>At the It meeting of 'Joe Uouncil the position of Vien-chairman was left ovn in order Co awertain if Mr Fult ,n Smith would accept the position. It now being understood thst he W 49 willin to fill the post, he was appointed vice-nhurn24n on Cho prop3sltlou of Mr Thompson, seconded by kir Taylor. THE COYONLTION.</p>
        <p>A discumion ensue -I wi-CU—ret-c-r-e-a-c-a to Vie propoted Col onation celebrations.</p>
        <p>The Clerk produeed a circol tr letter from the Local Government Board statinEz that the Board was pre pared 0 allow reasonabl3 expenses in con nection with such celebration out of the rates.</p>
        <p>The Chairman rein irkel that he did not altogether are with the suggestion to stind the ritepayers' ta*oey on a celebration and he thought it mi,g4t be done by voluntary effort. He imgested that voluntary subscriptions would be more desirable. -</p>
        <p>Mr danon, whikt n,rquggeitinr that tin rates should be used, exp eased the opinion that it was a more uni- form way of eubicrihing, fur when it wao left to volun• tsry effnrt the expense was borne by the few. I wie ultimately resolved that a parish meeting be called on Tuesday evening, M.y 20, to uiseuss the avuole</p>
