        <head>COMPLIMENT TO THE POLICE.</head>
        <p>A COMPLIMENT TO THE POLICE.</p>
        <p>Mr Halton incidentally referred to the alleged burglary at Sankey Board Scho,ls and to the clevr way the police at Great Sankey had effected tbe catraare of the prison- ers now in custody. Tne CI -rk was in.tructed to write to the Superinten- dent calling his attention to the matter and at the same time pointing out that the Cauncil were of opinion that a police constable should ho stationed near Sankey Church inread of having both the police sergeant and the constable located at Sankey Bridges. The Chairman explained that in the interview with the Superiarendent some time ago they merely requested that one police officer should be, located at the Sankey Bri ,gos end. Ho under,t )(el that Police Comtel•le Dug. dale had removed from Chapel-lane in consequence of the house being unsuitable for the requirements of his family.</p>
