        <p>The Leeds jury returned a verdict of " accidental death" in the case of Peter Conlon, a workmen in the employment of the Phoenix Foundry Co., Derby, who was killed on Monday while at work on the extensions to the electric lighting works in Whitehall-road. Con- lon was on a girder, and, losing bis balsoe, fiel a dis- tance of 321 t., breaking seven ribs and fracturing his skull. A strange story was revealed at an locrett on Wed- nesday, on a Norwich el neastian, John Westney, wko strangled himself in bed with a bit of etring. Aiebougb in fair health deceased had erected his own tombstone at the cemetery some time ago. His name was on the stone with verses beneath ; in feet, everything except the date of death. Flowers were also planted upon it, Westney having spent pounds on embellishing it.</p>
